@meta
id: 20-07
title: Drill — collect and put
chapter: 20
type: drill
skills: register-append
par: 30
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: cut a row, scroll, paste, scroll back, cut the other row, scroll, paste
open: orders.csv

@brief
Eight times: the two `FAILED` rows belong at the bottom of the file,
in their current order. Collect them into one register as you find
them and put them once.

@keys
| `"Add` | delete the line and append it to `a` |
| `n` | next match |
| `"ap` | put the collection |

@hints
`/FAILED` Enter, `"Add`, `n`, `"Add`. Then `G` and put.
--
The second delete leaves you on the last row already, so `G` is only
there in case the file was longer.

@solution
    /FAILED<Enter> "Add n"Add G"ap :wq<Enter>

Search, append-delete, next, append-delete, put. The pattern scales to
fifty rows without changing shape, and the register empties itself the
moment you start the next collection with a lowercase letter.

@start orders.csv
id,status
ord_001,PENDING
ord_002,FAILED
ord_003,SHIPPED
ord_004,FAILED
ord_005,PENDING
ord_006,SHIPPED

@expected orders.csv
id,status
ord_001,PENDING
ord_003,SHIPPED
ord_005,PENDING
ord_006,SHIPPED
ord_002,FAILED
ord_004,FAILED
